<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Potsdam Agreement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potsdam">Potsdam</a> Agreement was signed on 1 August 1945 at the end of the Potsdam Conference between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> and the United Kingdom. It set out the principles of the Allied occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, including demilitarisation, denazification, democratisation, decentralisation and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-reparations">reparations</a>, and approved the transfer of German populations from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>. It also placed the lands east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oder-neisse-line">Oder–Neisse line</a> under Polish and Soviet administration.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/potsdam-agreement.jpg" alt="Potsdam Agreement" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: US Government · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Clement_Attlee,_Harry_S._Truman,_and_Joseph_Stalin_at_the_Potsdam_Conference_1945,_NARA_(198950).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
